1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,517
Big exam, first date, going on stage… and your stomach starts to flutter.

2
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:09,346
That's your fight-or-flight response: your body gearing up to face a challenge.

3
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:12,760
1 — Your adrenal glands release adrenaline.

4
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:14,453
Heart and breathing speed up.

5
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:18,715
2 — Blood is sent away from your gut, toward your muscles.

6
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:26,754
3 — Digestion slows down and gut muscles change rhythm: that fluttery, queasy feeling.

7
00:00:27,450 --> 00:00:32,869
Your gut has its own nerve network, the “second brain,” wired to your brain by the vagus nerve.

8
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:35,849
It's a normal reaction, and it passes.

9
00:00:35,849 --> 00:00:38,007
Slow, deep breaths can help calm it.

10
00:00:38,710 --> 00:00:43,190
See a doctor if stomach symptoms are frequent or get in the way of daily life.
